As shown in the figure, it is the position–time graph (x–t graph) of a particle undergoing uniformly accelerated rectilinear motion, and P(t1, x1) is a point on the graph. PQ is the tangent line through point P, intersecting the x-axis at point Q(0, x2). It is known that when t=0, the magnitude of the particle's velocity is v0, then which of the following statements is correct?
A. At time t1, the particle's speed is $\frac{x_1}{t_1}
$B. At time t1, the particle's speed is $\frac{x_2}{t_1}\$C. The magnitude of the particle's acceleration is $\frac{x_{1}-x_{2}}{t_{1}^{2}}-\frac{v_{0}}{t_{1}}$D. The magnitude of the particle's acceleration is $1\frac{x_{1}-x_{2}}{t_{1}^{2}}$
